3c8ca5d1-d5fe-598d-8e92-88376fef649d" :question/math-academy-id "q-351795" :question/problem "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{4}(x)$ of $\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=1.$\n\n${P}_{4}(x)=2\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x-1)\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${(x-1)}^{2}\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n${(x-1)}^{3}\\,+\\,10{(x-1)}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=1,$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{3!}(x-1)^{3} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(1)}{4!}(x-1)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ ${f}^{‴}(1)$ and ${f}^{(4)}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=2{x}^{-2} & ⟹ &  & f(1) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-4{x}^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(1) & =-4 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{-4} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(1) & =12 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-48{x}^{-5} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(1) & =-48 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =240{x}^{-6} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}(1) & =240\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =2-4(x-1)+\\frac{12}{2!}(x-1)^{2}-\\frac{48}{3!}(x-1)^{3}+\\frac{240}{4!}(x-1)^{4} \\\\  & =2-4(x-1)+6(x-1)^{2}-8(x-1)^{3}+10(x-1)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351795/field-1" "q-351795/field-2" "q-351795/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22d992a1-2ea8-5226-9971-188447f98ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
